@startuml target_event_history_classes
title Target Event History - Shared Complete Projection
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' Source: campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventQueryService.java, list/pageOf.
' Source: campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java, toHistoryEvent/toSseData.
' Source: campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventCursorCodec.java, encode/decode.
' Observed behavior: current cursors have no fixed branch or upper watermark.
' Design reason: one complete projection prevents SSE/history identity drift.
' All new classes and relations are target-only; existing boundaries are changed.
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
package "Web boundary" {
  class RuntimeEventController <<singleton, existing-changed>>
  class ListSessionEventsRequestVO <<request, target-only>>
  class ListSessionEventsResponseVO <<immutable, target-only>>
  class SessionEventResponseVO <<immutable union, target-only>>
}
package "Application" {
  class SessionEventQueryService <<singleton, target-only>>
  class HistoryReadSnapshotDTO <<request immutable, target-only>>
  class HistoryCursorCodec <<singleton, target-only>>
  class CommittedEventProjection <<stateless singleton, target-only>>
  class RequestEventRouter <<singleton, target-only>>
}
package "Persistence boundary" {
  interface RuntimeSessionRepository <<existing-changed>>
  class MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository <<singleton, existing-changed>>
  class CommittedEventDTO <<immutable transfer, target-only>>
  class RuntimeSessionMapper <<singleton, existing-changed>>
}
RuntimeEventController --> ListSessionEventsRequestVO : validates
RuntimeEventController --> SessionEventQueryService : list
RuntimeEventController ..> ListSessionEventsResponseVO : returns
ListSessionEventsResponseVO *-- "0..*" SessionEventResponseVO : ordered events
SessionEventQueryService --> HistoryCursorCodec : validate / encode page
SessionEventQueryService ..> HistoryReadSnapshotDTO : resolves each request
SessionEventQueryService --> RuntimeSessionRepository : consistent read
SessionEventQueryService --> CommittedEventProjection : complete history
RequestEventRouter --> CommittedEventProjection : committed SSE only
CommittedEventProjection ..> CommittedEventDTO : reads
CommittedEventProjection ..> SessionEventResponseVO : creates
RuntimeSessionRepository <|.. MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository
MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository --> RuntimeSessionMapper
RuntimeSessionMapper ..> CommittedEventDTO : maps records
RuntimeSessionRepository ..> HistoryReadSnapshotDTO : fixed branch and bounds
note bottom of HistoryReadSnapshotDTO
  Binds branch, committed upper bound,
  position and visibility policy.
  No live database connection.
  Recheck current access on every page.
end note
note bottom of CommittedEventProjection
  Same eventId and complete payload for SSE and history.
  No credentials, raw delta or execution IDs.
  Not the execution-scoped SessionEventProjector.
end note
@enduml
@startuml target_event_history_paging
title Target Fixed Snapshot Paging - Oldest First Candidate
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' Source: campusclaw/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeSessionMapper.xml, listCurrentBranch.
' Source: campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventQueryService.java, list/pageOf.
' Observed behavior: each current query resolves active_leaf_id again.
' Design reason: fix branch and committed upper bound without a long transaction.
' Target-only architecture; page direction, limits and token lifetime remain candidates.
actor "Internal caller" as C
participant "History service" as Q
participant "Cursor codec" as T
database "Session / Event store" as D
participant "Execution appender" as A
C -> Q : GET events (limit, no page)
group Short consistent read transaction
  Q -> D : Check access / existence / visibility
  Q -> D : Read branch leaf and committed upper bound
  Q -> D : Read visible complete records (limit + 1)
  D --> Q : Snapshot and records
end
Q -> T : Encode bound continuation if more records
T --> Q : Opaque nextPage or null
Q --> C : ResultBean(events, nextPage)
A -> D : Commit new complete event after upper bound
note right of D : New records do not enter the earlier snapshot.
C -> Q : GET events (page = nextPage)
Q -> T : Verify session, integrity, expiry and versions
alt Valid token
  group Short consistent read transaction
    Q -> D : Recheck access, existence and visibility
    Q -> D : Read pinned branch within fixed upper bound
    D --> Q : Records or unavailable snapshot
  end
  alt Snapshot still readable
    Q -> T : Encode next position or return null
    Q --> C : Complete ordered events
  else Deleted / revoked / snapshot unavailable
    Q --> C : Error, never silently switch branch
  end
else Invalid token
  Q --> C : INVALID_EVENT_LIST_QUERY
end
note over C,Q
  null means snapshot exhausted, not execution finished.
  Start a fresh first page to include newer commits.
  No automatic replay of accepted POST requests.
end note
@enduml
